    "body": "Read/Edit should have one text-decoding policy. For invalid UTF-8, choose one behavior and surface it explicitly: reject as binary/invalid text with byte offset, or decode lossily with a flag and forbid Edit on lossy content.\n\nSilent replacement in Edit is dangerous because oldString matching can fail against a different byte sequence than the file actually contains. Tests should cover invalid byte in first chunk, later chunk, truncated multibyte sequence, and binary detection false negatives.\n\n---\n\n_Generated with [ax](https://github.com/Necmttn/ax)._\n",
